---
import PolicyPage from "@/components/layout/PolicyPage.astro";
import { signingCredit, signingTeam } from "@/data/policies";
import { site } from "@/data/site";

const roles = [
  { title: "Committers and reviewers", people: signingTeam.committers, note: "may change the code; changes from anyone else are reviewed in a pull request first." },
  { title: "Approvers", people: signingTeam.approvers, note: "approve each signing request by hand before a release is signed." },
];
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Code signing policy"
  description="Muelle's signing process, its current status, who approves signing requests, and what a signature does and does not guarantee."
  updated="November 16, 2026"
>
  <p>
    The latest published release, v0.1.8, is not Authenticode-signed: its GitHub Actions run skipped the SignPath
    steps. Until a release's signing steps complete, Windows may show a SmartScreen warning and will not display
    SignPath Foundation as its publisher. The <code>.sig</code> file attached to a release is for Muelle's updater;
    it is not an Authenticode signature.
  </p>
  <p>
    {signingCredit} Muelle has prepared a release workflow integration with the{" "}
    <a href="https://signpath.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SignPath Foundation</a> program for open
    source projects. A release is signed only when the workflow's SignPath steps run and finish successfully.
  </p>

  <h2>What gets signed when SignPath is enabled</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The installer (<code>Muelle-Setup.exe</code>) and the two programs it installs
      (<code>muelle.exe</code>, the dock, and <code>muelle-settings.exe</code>, Settings), built by the project's own{" "}
      <a href={`${site.repository}/blob/main/.github/workflows/release.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">release workflow</a>{" "}
      on GitHub-hosted runners, from the public source code in{" "}
      <a href={site.repository} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{site.repository.replace("https://", "")}</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Nothing built on a personal computer, and no third-party program is signed under this certificate.</li>
    <li>Every signed file is named Muelle and carries the version of the release it belongs to.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Team roles</h2>
  <ul>
    {
      roles.map(({ title, people, note }) => (
        <li>
          <b>{title}:</b>{" "}
          {people.map((person, index) => (
            <>
              {index > 0 && ", "}
              <a href={person.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                {person.name}
              </a>
            </>
          ))}
          {" "}— {note}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p>
    Signing requests require approval by an authorized approver. Before enabling signing, the project must confirm
    that the repository's access controls and multi-factor authentication meet SignPath Foundation's current
    requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This program will not transfer any information to other networked systems unless specifically
    requested by the user or the person installing or operating it. The exceptions are the update check
    and the optional AI usage island for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode Go, Gemini CLI,
    or Antigravity. They are described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and can be turned off in
    Settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Report a problem</h2>
  <p>
    If a Muelle release or its signature does something this page or the privacy policy does not describe, please{" "}
    <a href={site.issues} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open an issue</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
